WEBVTT

00:00:13.795 --> 00:00:15.797
&lt;i&gt;Welcome back
to theCerritos, Mr. Boimler.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:15.841 --> 00:00:18.800
When you were gone,
we tightened security protocols.

00:00:18.844 --> 00:00:21.020
If you run into any problems,
just flag it for Billups.

00:00:21.064 --> 00:00:23.457
Thank you, sir.
It's good to be back.

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:26.243
Computer, pupusa, hot.

00:00:26.286 --> 00:00:27.896
&lt;i&gt;User not recognized.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.942
It's Ensign Boimler. Come on.

00:00:29.985 --> 00:00:31.683
&lt;i&gt;User not recognized.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:31.726 --> 00:00:32.945
Can you, like, hurry it up?

00:00:32.988 --> 00:00:34.860
Computer, any food, hot, please.

00:00:34.903 --> 00:00:36.470
&lt;i&gt;User not recognized.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:39.908
-Hmm.
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:00:39.952 --> 00:00:41.910
What's the rush? We don't have
to report 'till 0800.

00:00:41.954 --> 00:00:43.564
There's a bunch I need to do
before my shift starts--

00:00:43.608 --> 00:00:44.913
recalibrate the omnidirectional restraints,

00:00:44.957 --> 00:00:46.524
prep the hyposprays...

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.134
Wait.
Is this about Ensign Escher?

00:00:48.178 --> 00:00:51.268
Yes! I can't believe she got
promoted over me. I do way more.

00:00:51.311 --> 00:00:52.747
Escher got lucky.

00:00:52.791 --> 00:00:54.836
I mean, curing the Captain's
Terellian Death Syndrome?

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.925
She was in the right place
with the right hypospray.

00:00:56.969 --> 00:00:58.840
Meh. I can't rely
on people getting syndromes.

00:00:58.884 --> 00:01:01.800
I have to show Dr. T'Ana
I've got what it takes.

00:01:01.843 --> 00:01:03.976
What up?
We doing sci-fi stuff today?

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:05.847
Uh, got to go
kick medical butt.

00:01:05.891 --> 00:01:09.590
Computer, ketchup, spicy kiwi.

00:01:13.855 --> 00:01:16.771
Mariner, are you seeing this?

00:01:16.815 --> 00:01:18.904
-Yeah, who messes with ketchup?

00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:21.036
-Shaxs is alive?
-Yeah, guess so.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.690
Bridge officers are always
coming back from the dead.

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:24.475
-You gonna finish that muffin?
-But how?

00:01:24.518 --> 00:01:26.303
He died in an explosion
saving my life.

00:01:26.346 --> 00:01:27.695
I don't know,
but whatever happened

00:01:27.739 --> 00:01:29.001
killed his taste buds for good.

00:01:29.044 --> 00:01:30.611
I mean, I don't have
all my memories,

00:01:30.655 --> 00:01:32.352
but I know for sure he saved me.

00:01:32.396 --> 00:01:34.006
They're gonna tell me
how he came back, right?

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:36.095
Nope. Best to not think
about it.

00:01:36.139 --> 00:01:37.662
&lt;i&gt;User not recognized.
-Please, just anything!&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:37.705 --> 00:01:39.751
I'm so hungry. Ah!

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.610
Ah.

00:02:56.654 --> 00:02:57.959
Ensign, get in here!

00:02:58.873 --> 00:03:00.571
I scrubbed half the arches,

00:03:00.614 --> 00:03:02.007
and I won't stop
until all the bile is...

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.530
Shut up. Listen.

00:03:03.574 --> 00:03:05.750
I need you to pick up
a... family heirloom

00:03:05.793 --> 00:03:07.752
from a-a storage unit
on Qualor II.

00:03:07.795 --> 00:03:10.581
-Wow! Dr. T'Ana, I'm honored!
-Ah, don't be.

00:03:10.624 --> 00:03:11.930
I just need
the lowest-ranking officer

00:03:11.973 --> 00:03:13.671
who will ask
the fewest questions.

00:03:13.714 --> 00:03:16.151
This is a personal mission.
Do it fast. Keep it private.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.589
You got it! And may I just
say I am so honored to...

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:21.722
Oh, go, go! Now! Go!

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:27.989
Ow! Stupid doors.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:29.774
Guess who I get to meet today.

00:03:29.817 --> 00:03:32.472
The Creator of Fair Haven,

00:03:32.516 --> 00:03:35.693
Lieutenant Tom Paris!

00:03:35.736 --> 00:03:38.609
No way! That's awesome!
Is he still a salamander?

00:03:38.652 --> 00:03:40.611
No, that's not...
It was a celerity-induced

00:03:40.654 --> 00:03:42.830
accelerated somatic mutation
rate, and he's fine now.

00:03:42.874 --> 00:03:44.963
He was the first human
to break the transwarp barrier,

00:03:45.006 --> 00:03:46.660
and today,
he's on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos!&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:46.704 --> 00:03:48.793
You have a &lt;i&gt;Voyager&lt;/i&gt; plate?

00:03:48.836 --> 00:03:50.838
I collect all sorts of plates,
and I love &lt;i&gt;Voy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:50.882 --> 00:03:53.145
See, I have signatures from
all the other bridge crew--

00:03:53.188 --> 00:03:56.148
from Janeway all the way down
to Kim! Everyone from &lt;i&gt;Voy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:56.191 --> 00:03:57.628
Why do you keep saying &lt;i&gt;"Voy"?&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:57.671 --> 00:03:58.977
That's what I call &lt;i&gt;Voyager
to save time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.457
-It doesn't.
-Paris is on a handshake tour,

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.806
telling &lt;i&gt;Voy&lt;/i&gt; stories for morale.

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:04.243
I heard Shaxs talking about it.

00:04:04.287 --> 00:04:06.506
It doesn't bug you
that he's back from the dead?

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.812
Eh, bridge crew always
come back.

00:04:07.855 --> 00:04:09.161
Fine, but how?

00:04:09.204 --> 00:04:10.641
-I don't know.
-We're Lower Decks.

00:04:10.684 --> 00:04:12.033
We don't get to know everything
bridge crew does.

00:04:12.077 --> 00:04:14.122
He saved my life. You know what?
I'm gonna ask him.

00:04:14.166 --> 00:04:15.994
They-they don't like when people
ask how they came back, man.

00:04:16.037 --> 00:04:17.996
It's probably just a transporter
pattern buffer thing.

00:04:18.039 --> 00:04:20.607
Yeah, or a restored katra, or
a mirror universe switcheroo,

00:04:20.651 --> 00:04:22.174
or the Borg rebuilt him.

00:04:22.217 --> 00:04:24.045
Or he could be a future son
from an alternate timeline,

00:04:24.089 --> 00:04:26.744
or maybe he got Genesis
Deviced, or time ribboned.

00:04:26.787 --> 00:04:29.529
-Or he was trapped in the Nexus.
-Nexus, time ribbon, same thing.

00:04:29.573 --> 00:04:32.097
Point is, this stuff always
happens, even on &lt;i&gt;Voy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.099
Wow. That does actually
save a ton of time.

00:04:34.142 --> 00:04:35.579
I'm an engineer.

00:04:35.622 --> 00:04:36.971
Solving impossible problems
is what I do.

00:04:37.015 --> 00:04:39.496
I can't let it go.

00:04:39.539 --> 00:04:42.194
And I can't let Tom Paris go,
not until he signs my plate.

00:04:43.238 --> 00:04:44.675
Damn it.

00:04:44.718 --> 00:04:46.111
This has been happening
all day.

00:04:46.154 --> 00:04:47.678
Yeah, they beefed up security
around here

00:04:47.721 --> 00:04:49.244
while you were gone
'cause of the Pakled attacks.

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:50.681
-Get Billups to put you
back in the system.

00:04:50.724 --> 00:04:53.205
I &lt;i&gt;am&lt;/i&gt; in the system.
It should be working.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.904
Ha!

00:04:56.948 --> 00:04:59.907
Mariner, hey! Dr. T'Ana just
gave me a super cool mission,

00:04:59.951 --> 00:05:01.735
and I can take someone along.
You want to come with?

00:05:01.779 --> 00:05:03.520
Wait. Me? Not Rutherford?

00:05:03.563 --> 00:05:05.043
Yeah, 'cause you know
what I realized?

00:05:05.086 --> 00:05:07.524
You and me have never done
a mission together.

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:08.960
What? No, we must have.

00:05:09.003 --> 00:05:11.049
-Nuh-uh, not just the two of us.
-Well, shoot, girl.

00:05:11.092 --> 00:05:13.051
Then it's about time.
Let's &lt;i&gt;do&lt;/i&gt; this!

00:05:13.094 --> 00:05:15.662
Mariner and Tendi on a...
girls' trip!

00:05:15.706 --> 00:05:17.838
Girls' trip!

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.669
Oh.

00:05:22.713 --> 00:05:25.063
-Computer, manual override. &lt;i&gt;
Request denied.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:25.106 --> 00:05:28.022
&lt;i&gt;-Unauthorized personnel.
Let me through!&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:28.066 --> 00:05:29.937
-What up, Boimler?
Need help with that door, buddy?

00:05:29.981 --> 00:05:31.156
No, I'm fine.

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:33.027
Hey, maybe you aren't back
in the system.

00:05:33.071 --> 00:05:35.160
I could carry you across
the threshold like a bride.

00:05:35.203 --> 00:05:36.596
Yeah, okay, Jet,
get out of here.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.945
I don't need you or anyone else

00:05:37.989 --> 00:05:39.730
to babysit me
through my own ship. I'm fine.

00:05:39.773 --> 00:05:41.035
All right, all right, all right.

00:05:41.079 --> 00:05:42.602
Aw.

00:05:42.646 --> 00:05:44.822
Mm, mm, mm.

00:05:48.956 --> 00:05:50.915
I'll show you unauthorized.

00:05:50.958 --> 00:05:55.310
Just... 200... more... rungs.

00:05:58.313 --> 00:06:00.272
&lt;i&gt;So weird we haven't
teamed up before now.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:00.315 --> 00:06:02.056
Sort of like
a glaring omission.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.580
You always get paired
with Boimler,

00:06:03.623 --> 00:06:04.929
and I'm always with Rutherford.

00:06:04.972 --> 00:06:06.104
We should switch it up
more often.

00:06:06.147 --> 00:06:08.323
Totally.
Qualor is awesome, by the way.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.238
You can get any drink
in the form of a slushie.

00:06:10.282 --> 00:06:12.676
&lt;i&gt;We got to get, like,
five slushies.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:12.719 --> 00:06:14.591
Dr. T'Ana seemed like
she wanted me to rush.

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.288
Who rushes a family heirloom?
It'll be fine.

00:06:16.331 --> 00:06:19.813
-It's like, old, right?
-Yeah, I-I guess you're right.

00:06:21.641 --> 00:06:22.990
Yeah!

00:06:23.034 --> 00:06:25.732
Whoa! Yeah!

00:06:27.299 --> 00:06:29.867
No one's accessed this bin
for years.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.172
You got authorization?

00:06:31.216 --> 00:06:32.826
Yup, right there.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:35.394
Is this Gik'Tal?
I love that song,

00:06:35.438 --> 00:06:37.614
where they sing over the wails
of the dishonored.

00:06:37.657 --> 00:06:39.050
"Gre'thor Paradise."

00:06:39.093 --> 00:06:41.792
Yeah, I saw them perform that
live on Akstin.

00:06:41.835 --> 00:06:43.141
They had an actual chorus

00:06:43.184 --> 00:06:46.100
of disgraced Klingons
lamenting on stage.

00:06:46.144 --> 00:06:48.886
-Oh, my gosh,
that sounds awesome!
-It was.

00:06:48.929 --> 00:06:51.323
I'll go poke around back there
and see what I can find.

00:06:51.366 --> 00:06:52.977
Shouldn't be long.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:55.849
Whoa. What? Stop.
You're into Klingon acid punk?

00:06:55.893 --> 00:06:57.634
Are you kidding?
Why even listen to Klingon

00:06:57.677 --> 00:06:59.157
if it isn't punky or acidic?

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.768
No way. I've never heard you
say anything about that.

00:07:01.812 --> 00:07:03.161
Well, that's weird,
because I talk

00:07:03.204 --> 00:07:04.815
to Rutherford about it
constantly.

00:07:04.858 --> 00:07:06.251
It's neat that after spending
all this time together,

00:07:06.294 --> 00:07:08.079
you can still learn something
about a friend.

00:07:08.122 --> 00:07:10.342
Yeah, I-I guess we just...

00:07:10.385 --> 00:07:13.040
All right.
Here you go.

00:07:13.084 --> 00:07:14.259
-Whoa.
-Whoa.

00:07:16.217 --> 00:07:18.350
Uh, when you said heirloom,
I thought it was going to be,

00:07:18.393 --> 00:07:20.700
like, a Caitian vase or
something. What is this exactly?

00:07:20.744 --> 00:07:22.441
I didn't ask.
Dr. T. is very private.

00:07:22.485 --> 00:07:24.704
Oh, let's open it up
and take a look.

00:07:24.748 --> 00:07:26.053
We really shouldn't.

00:07:26.097 --> 00:07:27.707
Come on!
Girls' trip!

00:07:27.751 --> 00:07:29.361
Come on.
One little peek won't hurt.

00:07:29.404 --> 00:07:31.972
It'll be our secret. We won't
even tell Boimler or Rutherford.

00:07:32.016 --> 00:07:35.149
-Mm, maybe just a quick
girls' peek.
-Girls' peek!

00:07:35.193 --> 00:07:37.021
Huh.

00:07:37.064 --> 00:07:38.805
It's just, like,
a wooden statue thingy?

00:07:38.849 --> 00:07:40.415
I wonder why
she's so wound up about this.

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:41.852
Oh, no.

00:07:41.895 --> 00:07:44.724
-What?
-It's not a statue.

00:07:44.768 --> 00:07:46.813
It's a Caitian Libido Post.

00:07:46.857 --> 00:07:49.207
Libido? Wait.
Oh, is that a sex thing?

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.426
A Caitian has to be...
intimate once a year,

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.950
or their hormones
make them crazy.

00:07:52.993 --> 00:07:54.429
It's like a Vulcan
on Pon Farr.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.257
Caitians have a bunch
of hormonal events like that.

00:07:56.301 --> 00:07:57.824
Ew.

00:07:57.868 --> 00:07:59.304
Oh, look at these claw marks.

00:07:59.347 --> 00:08:02.481
They're like, from her horny
great-grandma! Ew! Like...

00:08:02.525 --> 00:08:04.483
Hi, Tendi. Hi, Tendi.
My name is Jeremy.

00:08:04.527 --> 00:08:07.051
I'm an important cultural
sex toy from the past.

00:08:07.094 --> 00:08:09.227
-Please deliver me
to Dr. T'Ana so I...

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.881
Aah! I can't believe
you're touching it.

00:08:10.924 --> 00:08:12.839
Oh, my God, I'm touching it
with my bare hands.

00:08:12.883 --> 00:08:13.971
Put it back! put it back!
Put it back!

00:08:14.014 --> 00:08:15.102
Oh, just-just angle it
towards the...

00:08:15.146 --> 00:08:17.017
-Grab it!

00:08:24.459 --> 00:08:25.896
No, no, no, no, no!

00:08:25.939 --> 00:08:27.941
-This can't be happening!
-Well, maybe she won't

00:08:27.985 --> 00:08:29.334
-notice.
-It's the face!

00:08:29.377 --> 00:08:31.423
Dr. T'Ana's going to know
I violated her trust.

00:08:31.466 --> 00:08:33.077
I'm gonna get fired! Oh.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.775
Hey, no. Stop that. No. No one's
getting fired over Jeremy, okay?

00:08:35.819 --> 00:08:37.255
I've fixed stuff
like this before.

00:08:37.298 --> 00:08:38.735
You-you have?

00:08:38.778 --> 00:08:41.085
Yeah. No, I accidentally
ran over Worf's mek'leth

00:08:41.128 --> 00:08:42.739
back on Deep Space 9,
and I had it fixed

00:08:42.782 --> 00:08:44.175
before he even knew it was gone.

00:08:44.218 --> 00:08:46.394
What-what were you doing
on Deep Space 9?

00:08:46.438 --> 00:08:48.919
I served there back before I was
on the &lt;i&gt;Quito.&lt;/i&gt; You know that.

00:08:48.962 --> 00:08:51.182
No, I thought that the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos
was your first ship.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:51.225 --> 00:08:52.749
Seriously?
Dude, it's, like, my fifth.

00:08:52.792 --> 00:08:54.141
I talk about my other ships
all the time.

00:08:54.185 --> 00:08:56.013
Well, this is
the first I'm hearing about it.

00:08:56.056 --> 00:08:58.363
It's sort of a big part
of who I am.

00:08:58.406 --> 00:08:59.843
Uh, whatever.

00:08:59.886 --> 00:09:01.888
I know a fixer on Bonestell
who can repair anything.

00:09:01.932 --> 00:09:04.282
It's a quick warp, then we'll
head back to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:04.325 --> 00:09:06.284
with a nonruined post for T'Ana.

00:09:06.327 --> 00:09:07.546
Uh, okay.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:09.287
Well,
as long as we're back on time.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.767
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, we should be.

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.899
Yeah, uh, let's just get moving.

00:09:12.943 --> 00:09:15.293
&lt;i&gt;-Girls' trip.
Girls' trip.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:21.125 --> 00:09:23.127
-Rutherford.
-Sir.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.085
We've got
this Tom Paris thing later,

00:09:25.129 --> 00:09:27.087
but maybe after that,
racquetball?

00:09:27.131 --> 00:09:28.219
You sure you're up for that?

00:09:28.262 --> 00:09:29.829
You know,
with what you went through?

00:09:29.873 --> 00:09:32.919
Eh, that place
did take a lot out of me.

00:09:32.963 --> 00:09:35.487
-But not
my killer serve.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.358
Ah, Shaxs, you always get me.

00:09:37.402 --> 00:09:39.317
Help you, Ensign?

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:40.797
Oh.
I just...

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.103
The truth is
I was just wondering how...

00:09:43.147 --> 00:09:44.975
Whoa, Shaxs is back?

00:09:45.018 --> 00:09:47.804
Didn't you die? How the heck
did you come back to life?

00:09:47.847 --> 00:09:49.893
Oh.

00:09:49.936 --> 00:09:52.547
Lieutenant Junior Grade Cody,
that is out of line!

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:55.420
Report to your supervisor
for immediate reassignment.

00:09:55.463 --> 00:09:57.030
I'm sorry. I-I didn't mean to...

00:09:57.074 --> 00:09:59.206
Just go.

00:10:00.207 --> 00:10:01.556
But he &lt;i&gt;was&lt;/i&gt; dead. I...

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:05.996
What was it you wanted to ask?

00:10:06.039 --> 00:10:07.998
Oh, uh, uh...

00:10:08.041 --> 00:10:10.522
Uh, how do you hit
a racquetball?

00:10:10.565 --> 00:10:12.219
With a racket.

00:10:12.263 --> 00:10:14.831
Oh! Right. Cool.

00:10:14.874 --> 00:10:16.571
So, you, uh,
still having flashbacks?

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:19.183
Having one right now.

00:10:23.143 --> 00:10:24.449
Yeah, I can fix it. The trick is

00:10:24.492 --> 00:10:26.320
making it look
like it was never damaged.

00:10:26.364 --> 00:10:27.582
And how much
will that put us back?

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:29.454
For my old friend
Beckett Mariner?

00:10:29.497 --> 00:10:31.412
Double. 50 strips.

00:10:31.456 --> 00:10:34.024
What-- 50? Where are we supposed
to find that much latinum?

00:10:34.067 --> 00:10:35.852
You've got a deal.

00:10:35.895 --> 00:10:37.549
What are you doing?
We can't afford that.

00:10:37.592 --> 00:10:39.246
Yes, we can.
We just need to find

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:40.595
the biggest,
dumbest guys in here.

00:10:45.252 --> 00:10:47.951
Come on, come on.

00:10:49.082 --> 00:10:51.084
Cheater!

00:10:51.128 --> 00:10:53.391
You claimed
you were only a beginner.

00:10:53.434 --> 00:10:55.959
Yeah, I'm &lt;i&gt;beginning
to school your ugly ass.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:56.002 --> 00:10:57.917
-How dare you!
-Hey! No fighting.

00:10:57.961 --> 00:10:59.876
I just got that table rejotted.

00:10:59.919 --> 00:11:02.487
You want to finish this game,
you do it with proxies.

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:05.185
Works for me. My partner's
even better than I am.

00:11:05.229 --> 00:11:08.493
An Orion? She will use
her pheromones to cheat us.

00:11:08.536 --> 00:11:10.408
No, she won't.

00:11:10.451 --> 00:11:13.019
Oh, that is
such a messed up thing to say.

00:11:13.063 --> 00:11:15.326
But, like, could you, you know,
just, like, juice it a bit?

00:11:15.369 --> 00:11:16.893
-Just a little?
Mariner!

00:11:16.936 --> 00:11:18.459
Of course not.
I'm not even that kind of Orion.

00:11:18.503 --> 00:11:20.331
I can't believe
you'd even say that.

00:11:20.374 --> 00:11:22.246
Uh, just checking.
No, no. No, you got this.

00:11:22.289 --> 00:11:23.377
-Take a shot.

00:11:24.422 --> 00:11:25.902
Uh...

00:11:25.945 --> 00:11:27.077
Uh... Come on.

00:11:31.037 --> 00:11:33.126
-I won?

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.519
I won!

00:11:34.562 --> 00:11:36.260
-Yeah!
Dom-jot! Dom-jot!

00:11:36.303 --> 00:11:37.914
All right, pay up.

00:11:37.957 --> 00:11:40.917
Cheaters don't deserve
Nausicaan latinum.

00:11:42.657 --> 00:11:44.529
No!

00:11:44.572 --> 00:11:47.053
-Hey! What'd I say
about... Whoa!

00:11:47.097 --> 00:11:48.489
Oh, crap! Okay, guys, listen.

00:11:48.533 --> 00:11:49.969
I know we may not look
like a lot,

00:11:50.013 --> 00:11:51.144
but when it comes to a fight,

00:11:51.188 --> 00:11:52.624
us Starfleet officers
are trained to...

00:11:52.667 --> 00:11:53.930
-Latinum!

00:11:53.973 --> 00:11:55.496
Tendi, run!

00:12:01.981 --> 00:12:03.678
If I follow this path,
I'll be on the catwalk

00:12:03.722 --> 00:12:05.985
above the grav stabilizer's
static diffusers.

00:12:06.029 --> 00:12:08.466
Almost to the bridge.
Don't worry, plate.

00:12:08.509 --> 00:12:10.468
There's no plausible reason
why anyone should be purging

00:12:10.511 --> 00:12:12.035
the static right now.

00:12:15.212 --> 00:12:17.997
It's a pleasure to have you
on my bridge, Lieutenant Paris.

00:12:18.041 --> 00:12:19.956
Pleasure's all mine,
Captain Freeman.

00:12:19.999 --> 00:12:21.653
Mind if I give her a whirl?
I hear

00:12:21.696 --> 00:12:24.351
-these Cali-class engines
can purr.
-Of course.

00:12:24.395 --> 00:12:26.397
Just don't send us
to the Delta Quadrant.

00:12:28.094 --> 00:12:30.009
All right.

00:12:30.053 --> 00:12:32.490
Oh, no. Oh, no.

00:12:36.233 --> 00:12:37.495
Computer, emergency shutdown!

00:12:37.538 --> 00:12:39.062
&lt;i&gt;Authorization not recognized.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:39.105 --> 00:12:42.630
You don't need authorization
in an emergency!

00:12:43.675 --> 00:12:46.373
Ah, my plate. Okay.

00:12:46.417 --> 00:12:49.028
She's okay.
Aah! Hot plate. Ow, my lips.

00:12:49.072 --> 00:12:50.551
Okay, I'm fine.
The plate is fine.

00:12:50.595 --> 00:12:52.336
Got to keep moving.

00:12:54.381 --> 00:12:55.992
Where the hell are you, Ensign?

00:12:56.035 --> 00:12:58.168
&lt;i&gt;My fur feels
like it's covered in poison.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:58.211 --> 00:13:00.561
We're on our way back.
The package is completely intact

00:13:00.605 --> 00:13:02.128
-and... &lt;i&gt;
-Hurry!&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:02.172 --> 00:13:04.174
This was supposed to be
my chance

00:13:04.217 --> 00:13:07.133
to show Dr. T'Ana that I'm ready
for more, but I failed her!

00:13:07.177 --> 00:13:08.569
Uh, look,
don't be so hard on yourself.

00:13:08.613 --> 00:13:10.180
-It was just a mistake.
-I don't get

00:13:10.223 --> 00:13:11.790
to make mistakes like you do.

00:13:11.834 --> 00:13:13.487
It was hard
getting into the Academy.

00:13:13.531 --> 00:13:15.315
There's still a lot of stigma
around Orions.

00:13:15.359 --> 00:13:18.405
A lot of humans think
we're all thieves and pirates.

00:13:18.449 --> 00:13:19.754
Wait.

00:13:19.798 --> 00:13:21.234
My cousin works
in a thieves' den

00:13:21.278 --> 00:13:22.714
in a pirate outpost
in this sector.

00:13:22.757 --> 00:13:24.368
-He might be able
to help us out.
-Uh, okay.

00:13:24.411 --> 00:13:26.370
As long as you aren't bothered
by the optics,

00:13:26.413 --> 00:13:28.024
-I mean, it works for me.

00:13:28.067 --> 00:13:29.677
Well, these are bad Orions.

00:13:29.721 --> 00:13:32.071
They'd kill you on the spot
just for being human.

00:13:32.115 --> 00:13:35.770
-Well, I'm not into that.
-But don't worry, I have a plan.

00:13:35.814 --> 00:13:40.297
All right, undercover op.

00:13:48.348 --> 00:13:50.568
Just got to focus on work.

00:13:50.611 --> 00:13:52.091
Come on. Focus.

00:13:52.135 --> 00:13:54.702
Rutherford. I fought my way
out of the multiverse.

00:13:54.746 --> 00:13:57.792
That is a lie. The Borg
put my body into the Collective.

00:13:57.836 --> 00:14:00.230
You...

00:14:00.273 --> 00:14:03.537
A microscopic civilization
brought me back to life

00:14:03.581 --> 00:14:06.584
to harness the powers of my body
with a tiny Dyson sphere.

00:14:06.627 --> 00:14:09.195
-Uh...
-It was no transporter accident.

00:14:09.239 --> 00:14:11.284
-Resistance is futile.
-Mirror, mirror, mirror.

00:14:11.328 --> 00:14:13.765
What was the deal with T'Pol's
hair for that one year?

00:14:13.808 --> 00:14:15.593
-In the Nexus,
it's always Christmas.

00:14:15.636 --> 00:14:16.811
I got to know!

00:14:27.474 --> 00:14:29.607
Honestly, this feels wrong.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.609
I mean, just please don't take
any pictures of me.

00:14:31.652 --> 00:14:33.741
Okay, remember,
the effect won't last long,

00:14:33.785 --> 00:14:35.613
so we need to find D'Onni quick.

00:14:35.656 --> 00:14:38.790
Well, what if I don't sound
like an Orion, though?

00:14:38.833 --> 00:14:40.661
Just talk like a pirate.

00:14:41.706 --> 00:14:44.752
Arr, how ye
be doing today, me fellow Orion?

00:14:44.796 --> 00:14:47.277
Uh, why are you talking
like that?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.713
-Allergies.
Yeah,
I'm allergic

00:14:48.756 --> 00:14:50.541
to, um, uh, pheromones.

00:14:50.584 --> 00:14:51.672
-Oh, I hear you.

00:14:51.716 --> 00:14:53.239
They're really bad
this time of year.

00:14:53.283 --> 00:14:55.589
That's D'Onni up there.

00:14:55.633 --> 00:14:59.332
-He does art forgeries.
-Uh, and he's hot?

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.509
Tendi, you got to warn me
if we're gonna be meeting up

00:15:02.553 --> 00:15:03.815
with a sexy bad boy.

00:15:03.858 --> 00:15:05.338
That's my type.
Well, one of my types.

00:15:05.382 --> 00:15:06.818
You have a thing for bad boys?

00:15:06.861 --> 00:15:08.776
Oh, I'm always dating bad boys,

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:10.735
bad girls,
bad gender nonbinary babes,

00:15:10.778 --> 00:15:13.129
ruthless alien masterminds,
bad Bynars.

00:15:13.172 --> 00:15:15.653
Huh. I don't know if I've
ever seen you date anyone.

00:15:15.696 --> 00:15:17.263
You usually seem to be
with Boimler.

00:15:17.307 --> 00:15:19.309
What? Ew, no! What?

00:15:19.352 --> 00:15:21.615
-Ew, that is so messed up.
-What? I don't know. You guys

00:15:21.659 --> 00:15:23.313
practically sleep
in the same bunk.

00:15:23.356 --> 00:15:24.836
Ew, we do not! Ew!

00:15:24.879 --> 00:15:26.664
He's like a pet. Yuck.

00:15:26.707 --> 00:15:28.144
What, are you
and Rutherford dating?

00:15:28.187 --> 00:15:29.623
Not really.
-Cousin?

00:15:29.667 --> 00:15:32.191
Biceps.

00:15:32.235 --> 00:15:34.585
You shouldn't be here.
If the Syndicate catches me

00:15:34.628 --> 00:15:36.326
-talking to...
-You'll do
what I tell you to do,

00:15:36.369 --> 00:15:38.197
you dumb-face jerk!

00:15:39.416 --> 00:15:41.374
-Holy crap,
who are you right now?
-It's an Orion thing.

00:15:41.418 --> 00:15:43.159
It actually makes me
really uncomfortable.

00:15:43.202 --> 00:15:45.900
D'Onni, I have a piece of, uh,
loot I need you to repair.

00:15:45.944 --> 00:15:47.859
It has to look like
it was never broken in order

00:15:47.902 --> 00:15:49.774
to rip someone off.

00:15:49.817 --> 00:15:52.646
Anything for you, Mistress
of the Winter Constellations.

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:54.605
Mistress of the Winter Constella...?

00:15:54.648 --> 00:15:56.694
What? Okay, you got to do this
on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:56.737 --> 00:15:59.349
Don't tell anyone. That's a name
I left behind long ago.

00:15:59.392 --> 00:16:00.698
I'll try, but it's...

00:16:00.741 --> 00:16:03.875
-Oh, crap.
-D'Vana, what is this?

00:16:03.918 --> 00:16:06.660
-Is she an imposter?
-Shut up and do your job!

00:16:06.704 --> 00:16:09.533
"D'Vana"? Is that some other
weird title you've got?

00:16:09.576 --> 00:16:11.274
It's my name.

00:16:11.317 --> 00:16:12.797
-Oh.
What,

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:15.278
you don't even know
my first name?

00:16:15.321 --> 00:16:16.366
I thought it was Tendi,

00:16:16.409 --> 00:16:18.194
like, with no last name.
Like Odo.

00:16:18.237 --> 00:16:20.935
We have been working together
for over a year, Beckett.

00:16:20.979 --> 00:16:23.373
-Well, now you're
just showing off.
-You don't know me at all.

00:16:23.416 --> 00:16:25.984
-Well, &lt;i&gt;you&lt;/i&gt; don't know &lt;i&gt;me.
-Hey! You don't have allergies!&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:26.028 --> 00:16:27.420
Uh...

00:16:27.464 --> 00:16:29.553
She's wearing false green!
Grab her!

00:16:39.954 --> 00:16:41.869
-Get her!

00:16:41.913 --> 00:16:44.742
-False green! False green!

00:16:44.785 --> 00:16:45.786
Run!

00:16:50.748 --> 00:16:52.228
Why don't you just do

00:16:52.271 --> 00:16:53.533
your "bossing everyone around"
voice again?

00:16:53.577 --> 00:16:55.361
Yeah, it doesn't work
on angry mobs.

00:16:55.405 --> 00:16:58.234
Which you would know if you knew
anything about me &lt;i&gt;or&lt;/i&gt; Orions.

00:16:58.277 --> 00:16:59.800
You're the one who wanted
to do a girls' trip.

00:16:59.844 --> 00:17:01.411
Because I thought
we were friends!

00:17:01.454 --> 00:17:02.455
Yeah, well, apparently,

00:17:02.499 --> 00:17:03.500
we're just people
who work together.

00:17:03.543 --> 00:17:04.718
Yeah, soon we'll just be people

00:17:04.762 --> 00:17:05.937
who get our asses kicked
together.

00:17:14.293 --> 00:17:16.034
They're all over the lift.

00:17:19.951 --> 00:17:21.692
Hope you like climbing.

00:17:24.999 --> 00:17:27.785
Ha! Nobody knows the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos
like Bradward Boimler.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:27.828 --> 00:17:30.614
Fine. You want
to play it that way, &lt;i&gt;Cerritos?&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:30.657 --> 00:17:32.398
I know another way.
Because I know you,

00:17:32.442 --> 00:17:33.791
like you should know &lt;i&gt;me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:33.834 --> 00:17:35.532
&lt;i&gt;Access denied.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:35.575 --> 00:17:37.403
Oh, no, no, no.
This can't be happening.

00:17:37.447 --> 00:17:38.796
First I get kicked off
the &lt;i&gt;Titan.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:38.839 --> 00:17:40.624
Then the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos
doesn't even know me anymore?&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:40.667 --> 00:17:43.061
Where do I belong?
Aw.

00:17:44.802 --> 00:17:47.370
Come on, Brad.
This is your home.

00:17:47.413 --> 00:17:48.675
You're right where you belong.

00:17:48.719 --> 00:17:50.721
Then why am I gonna die
in a Jefferies tube?

00:17:50.764 --> 00:17:53.854
You're not.
You are Brad Boimler.

00:17:53.898 --> 00:17:55.856
And you've been
in tougher spots than this.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.816
Now open up a panel and
start figuring out a solution.

00:17:58.859 --> 00:18:00.296
You're right.

00:18:00.339 --> 00:18:01.645
Thanks, Tom Paris.

00:18:04.038 --> 00:18:06.563
-I am a little worried
about the fumes in here though.

00:18:06.606 --> 00:18:08.434
-You know,
since you're talking to a plate.

00:18:08.478 --> 00:18:10.958
I don't know. I kinda like 'em.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.531
There!

00:18:18.575 --> 00:18:19.924
Don't let 'em get away!

00:18:27.105 --> 00:18:29.020
Leave us alone!
This isn't nice!

00:18:29.063 --> 00:18:30.630
Yes. Wait, no!

00:18:30.674 --> 00:18:31.675
-Keep cutting!

00:18:44.688 --> 00:18:46.516
The post. It's too heavy.

00:18:46.559 --> 00:18:47.778
I can't pull you both up!

00:18:50.476 --> 00:18:51.956
Take it! Get out of here

00:18:51.999 --> 00:18:53.087
-before it's too late!

00:18:53.131 --> 00:18:54.741
No way! I'm not leaving you!

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:57.570
-Tendi, no!

00:18:57.614 --> 00:18:59.529
-Not the post!

00:19:12.411 --> 00:19:13.978
-Deck 15.
-Wait!

00:19:17.721 --> 00:19:19.636
Whoa. Baby Bear.
What's the matter?

00:19:19.679 --> 00:19:20.680
I know I'm not supposed
to ask you

00:19:20.724 --> 00:19:21.855
how you came back from the dead,

00:19:21.899 --> 00:19:23.596
but I know it was my fault
that you died.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:24.902
And maybe if you tell me
how you came back,

00:19:24.945 --> 00:19:26.382
I won't feel as guilty anymore!

00:19:26.425 --> 00:19:27.600
Turbolift, halt.

00:19:28.645 --> 00:19:30.690
It wasn't your fault.

00:19:30.734 --> 00:19:32.605
Saving you was my duty.

00:19:32.649 --> 00:19:35.521
There's a reason we don't tell
anyone how we come back.

00:19:35.565 --> 00:19:38.002
I know. You can't tell me
because I'm just an ensign.

00:19:38.045 --> 00:19:39.786
It's nothing to do with rank,
son.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:43.660
We're sparing you dark truths
about scientific depravity

00:19:43.703 --> 00:19:46.489
that would haunt you
for the rest of your days.

00:19:46.532 --> 00:19:48.012
Once you know,

00:19:48.055 --> 00:19:52.059
you can never go back to being
the man you were before.

00:19:52.103 --> 00:19:53.713
Works for me! Tell me, tell me!

00:19:53.757 --> 00:19:56.542
Okay. So, death is
the first thing that happens.

00:19:56.586 --> 00:19:59.023
And then-- Oh, wait, you do know
about the black mountain, right?

00:19:59.066 --> 00:20:01.025
-Uh, the what now?
-The black mountain

00:20:01.068 --> 00:20:03.723
is a spiritual battleground
your soul goes

00:20:03.767 --> 00:20:04.942
where you have to fight

00:20:04.985 --> 00:20:07.901
three faceless apparitions
of your father.

00:20:07.945 --> 00:20:10.861
...the surviving father
makes you eat your heart...

00:20:13.167 --> 00:20:14.995
I'm trapped
because of a computer glitch,

00:20:15.039 --> 00:20:17.781
or perhaps it is I
who is the glitch.

00:20:17.824 --> 00:20:20.087
&lt;i&gt;Personal log cannot be recorded.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:20.131 --> 00:20:21.741
I'm gonna die

00:20:21.785 --> 00:20:23.003
and it's all
because of this stupid plate!

00:20:23.047 --> 00:20:24.614
-Don't do it, Bradward!

00:20:24.657 --> 00:20:26.616
-Not the plate!

00:20:26.659 --> 00:20:28.705
Uh, huh? Oh, God.

00:20:28.748 --> 00:20:30.924
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!

00:20:33.492 --> 00:20:36.147
I... do exist!

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.062
-Tom Paris!
-A Kazon!

00:20:38.105 --> 00:20:40.194
Tom Paris, can I just say that
I'm a really huge fan and I have

00:20:40.238 --> 00:20:41.892
-a plate for you...

00:20:44.634 --> 00:20:46.723
Thanks for saving
my ass back there.

00:20:46.766 --> 00:20:48.638
You've saved mine plenty
of times.

00:20:48.681 --> 00:20:50.161
I'm sorry you brought me
instead of Rutherford.

00:20:50.204 --> 00:20:51.728
But, you know, don't feel bad

00:20:51.771 --> 00:20:52.990
that you don't know much
about my life.

00:20:53.033 --> 00:20:54.600
I keep it vague on purpose.

00:20:54.644 --> 00:20:55.601
Well, why?

00:20:55.645 --> 00:20:57.473
Every time I open up,

00:20:57.516 --> 00:20:59.083
people get promoted
and take off.

00:20:59.126 --> 00:21:00.867
It's better
to just keep it surface level

00:21:00.911 --> 00:21:01.868
and never have friends,

00:21:01.912 --> 00:21:03.261
instead of always losing them.

00:21:03.305 --> 00:21:04.828
Well, don't apologize.

00:21:04.871 --> 00:21:06.786
I was hoping this trip
would be a way for us to bond,

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:08.832
but it's just been a big mess.

00:21:08.875 --> 00:21:10.703
And the reason
you don't know much about me?

00:21:10.747 --> 00:21:13.271
That's my fault. I'm always so
busy making everyone else happy

00:21:13.315 --> 00:21:14.794
that I never open up.

00:21:14.838 --> 00:21:16.709
Now you know more about me
than Rutherford does.

00:21:16.753 --> 00:21:17.841
And I'm glad I do.

00:21:17.884 --> 00:21:19.233
Me, too.

00:21:20.234 --> 00:21:22.498
What are you gonna tell the doc?

00:21:22.541 --> 00:21:24.935
That I was curious
and accidentally broke her post.

00:21:24.978 --> 00:21:26.676
It'll be interesting
getting in trouble.

00:21:26.719 --> 00:21:28.112
I've never done that before.

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:31.637
you're a really good person.

00:21:31.681 --> 00:21:32.638
Aw, thanks.

00:21:32.682 --> 00:21:33.683
What's the other thing?

00:21:33.726 --> 00:21:35.293
Your plan sucks. New plan.

00:21:35.337 --> 00:21:36.947
Oh, my gosh.

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:38.601
-What are you doing?
-Buckle up, D'Vana.

00:21:38.644 --> 00:21:40.211
We might have been coworkers
this morning,

00:21:40.254 --> 00:21:41.865
but now we're friends!

00:21:41.908 --> 00:21:44.737
Computer, ramming speed!

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.653
Friendship!

00:21:47.697 --> 00:21:49.699
This is how we kick ass
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:21:49.742 --> 00:21:50.700
Ki-ya!

00:21:54.573 --> 00:21:56.967
Uh, Captain, Shuttle Four
is on a collision course

00:21:57.010 --> 00:21:58.098
-with the ship.
What?

00:21:58.142 --> 00:21:59.099
Uh...

00:21:59.143 --> 00:22:00.710
Stop! Stop!

00:22:04.583 --> 00:22:05.845
Damage report?

00:22:05.889 --> 00:22:06.846
None.

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:08.108
That was weird.

00:22:12.286 --> 00:22:13.766
What the hell were you thinking?

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:15.202
A bee got in the shuttle, sir.

00:22:15.246 --> 00:22:17.683
It flew right in my face.
Totally my fault.

00:22:17.727 --> 00:22:21.252
A bee? How did a bee get
in the shuttle &lt;i&gt;in space?!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:22.601 --> 00:22:25.561
Dr. T'Ana, I'm so sorry,

00:22:25.604 --> 00:22:27.563
but I'm afraid your special
family heirloom is broken.

00:22:27.606 --> 00:22:29.260
And I wish I could say that it
was because of something else,

00:22:29.303 --> 00:22:30.653
-but...
Totally my fault.

00:22:30.696 --> 00:22:32.089
Sorry, Doc.
Big old bee got in the shuttle.

00:22:32.132 --> 00:22:33.264
Just messed everything up.

00:22:33.307 --> 00:22:35.005
You are so going
to the brig for this.

00:22:35.048 --> 00:22:37.094
Send the bee to the brig!
It's the bee's fault!

00:22:37.137 --> 00:22:38.791
I'm really sorry.

00:22:38.835 --> 00:22:41.011
Don't worry about it.

00:22:41.054 --> 00:22:42.055
W-- You're not mad?

00:22:43.753 --> 00:22:45.276
I don't care
about that old post.

00:22:45.319 --> 00:22:47.321
What I needed was the box.

00:22:54.328 --> 00:22:56.069
Mmm.

00:22:56.113 --> 00:22:58.245
There's-- That's the stuff.

00:23:01.901 --> 00:23:03.163
Ooh, have you heard this one?

00:23:03.207 --> 00:23:04.251
It's my favorite.

00:23:04.295 --> 00:23:06.079
It's all
about the Caves of No'Mat.

00:23:06.123 --> 00:23:08.299
Acid punkers love singing
about caves!

00:23:08.342 --> 00:23:09.779
-Oh, hello.

00:23:09.822 --> 00:23:11.607
Check it out. No more glitch.

00:23:11.650 --> 00:23:13.086
I'm authorized!

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:16.002
Did you get your bowl signed
by Chakotay or whatever?

00:23:16.046 --> 00:23:18.004
Tom Paris. And, no, not yet.

00:23:18.048 --> 00:23:21.007
But this black eye he gave me is
way cooler than a signed plate.

00:23:21.051 --> 00:23:22.748
True. There's, like,
only a couple of people

00:23:22.792 --> 00:23:24.924
in the quadrant who can say
they got beat up by Tom Paris.

00:23:24.968 --> 00:23:27.405
Even better, as an apology,
we're getting drinks tonight.

00:23:27.449 --> 00:23:29.712
So I still have a chance
for him to sign it.

00:23:31.278 --> 00:23:32.802
Oh, no. No, no, no,
no, no, no, no!

00:23:32.845 --> 00:23:33.846
Computer, open the door!

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.369
I got to get to the bar!
Come on!

00:23:35.413 --> 00:23:36.849
Uh, that's-that's not a door.

00:23:36.893 --> 00:23:38.372
It's just a wall with a seam.

00:23:38.416 --> 00:23:41.332
Oh. Right.
I may have a concussion.

00:23:41.375 --> 00:23:44.335
-Oh, Rutherford, did you ever
find out how Shaxs came back?

00:23:44.378 --> 00:23:45.989
Oh.

00:23:46.032 --> 00:23:48.165
No. No, I did not.

00:23:48.208 --> 00:23:50.297
Aw, boo. We never get to know
the cool stuff.

00:23:50.341 --> 00:23:52.169
Or maybe they're just sparing us
from knowing

00:23:52.212 --> 00:23:55.825
horrible, horrible things
that-that happen to good people.

00:23:55.868 --> 00:23:57.696
Yea, it definitely isn't that.
They're just jerks.

00:23:57.740 --> 00:23:59.698
Ooh, this one's about a Klingon
who eats his own hand.

00:23:59.742 --> 00:24:00.960
Yeah, play it!

00:24:03.049 --> 00:24:05.399
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:25:04.067 --> 00:25:06.025
Chirp.
